          "type": "LinguisticObject",
          "content": "Japanese colonial rule of Korea (1910–1945). The colonial language policy — forbidding Korean while enforcing Japanese — forms a central historical context for the text's engagement with linguistic displacement and intergenerational loss.",
          "classified_as": "description"
        },
        {
          "type": "LinguisticObject",
          "content": "1910-1945. Mother's language prohibition: 'They say you spoke in tongue forbidden' (p.45). Yu Gwan-sun's imprisonment and death. Structural context for translational violence across generations.",
          "classified_as": "scope_note"
        }
      ],
